comments.message:
@Matt & @Ed
As part of this PR i am trying to define a way the pre and post conditions can be triggered for firmware update. The approach i am suggesting here is to define a platform json configuration with systemd targets. 
Another approach could be to add these targets to EM schema definitions. But as per my earlier conversation with @Matt, he had suggested me to avoid using systemd targets in EM configurations. Can you please provide more details on that intent on why systemd targets are not preferred in EM configurations?

@spinler@us.ibm.com 

>For example, one wouldn't hardcode d-bus service names or object paths in EM config files.

Thanks, can we add it as FAQ/Best Practices in entity-manager also the rationale for not allowing. On a quick search, I couldn't find this.
